<%#- STRUCTURAL fork, not a class swap. DaisyUI's `join-item btn` is already an
     abstraction, so its six item variants can repeat two tokens inline. Plain
     Tailwind has no component class, so the shared item styling has to become a
     template LOCAL — otherwise fourteen utilities appear six times and a tweak
     has to be made six times. A class-token map cannot express that.

     Emitted ONCE per app into app/views/shared/, so nothing here may name the
     resource: everything resource-shaped (the wrapper id, the anchor target,
     the page-number window) arrives as a local from the list partial. The
     `--css=` marker below is how a later scaffold run detects a variant
     mismatch — keep it. -%>
<%%# locals: (page: 1, page_count: 1, pages: [], anchor:, id:) -%>
<%%# Shared page control (--css=<%= css_variant %>), rendered above and below
    every scaffolded list. The links are anchors to the list, so a click also
    does the browser's own fragment jump; data-turbo="false" keeps Turbo Drive
    out. `on` returns a { data: } hash — merge, don't splat, or the anchor
    stops scrolling. %>
<%% page_data = ->(n) { { turbo: false }.merge(on(:go_to_page, with: { page: n })[:data]) } %>
<%% item = "relative inline-flex items-center border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium first:rounded-l-md last:rounded-r-md" %>
<%% item_link = "#{item} bg-white text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-50" %>
<%% item_current = "#{item} z-10 bg-indigo-600 border-indigo-600 text-white" %>
<%% item_inert = "#{item} bg-white text-gray-300 cursor-not-allowed" %>
<%%# The wrapper always renders (so idiomorph has a node to pair with) and
    stays bare — layout classes here would leave dead space when empty. %>
<div id="<%%= id %>">
  <%% if page_count > 1 %>
    <nav<%= css_attr(:pagination_nav) %> aria-label="Pagination">
      <%%# Prev/next go inert at the ends rather than disappearing, so the
          control keeps its width across a page change. %>
      <%% if page == 1 %>
        <span class="<%%= item_inert %>" aria-disabled="true">«</span>
      <%% else %>
        <%%= link_to "«", anchor, class: item_link, rel: "prev",
                    "aria-label": "Previous page", data: page_data.(page - 1) %>
      <%% end %>

      <%% pages.each do |n| %>
        <%% if n.nil? %>
          <span class="<%%= item_inert %>" aria-hidden="true">…</span>
        <%% elsif n == page %>
          <span class="<%%= item_current %>" aria-current="page"><%%= n %></span>
        <%% else %>
          <%%= link_to n, anchor, class: item_link,
                      "aria-label": "Page #{n}", data: page_data.(n) %>
        <%% end %>
      <%% end %>

      <%% if page == page_count %>
        <span class="<%%= item_inert %>" aria-disabled="true">»</span>
      <%% else %>
        <%%= link_to "»", anchor, class: item_link, rel: "next",
                    "aria-label": "Next page", data: page_data.(page + 1) %>
      <%% end %>
    </nav>
  <%% end %>
</div>
